{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Shem, Ham, and Japheth.</b> It appears to me that Japheth is the firstborn, as it is said (Genesis 10:21), \"the brother of Japheth the elder,\" and so he lists them according to their generations: the sons of Japheth first (ibid. v. 2). And Ham is the youngest of them all, as he said (ibid. 9:24), \"and he knew what his youngest son had done to him.\" But he placed Shem first on account of his distinction, and he mentioned Ham after him, for that is the order in which they were born — and so Japheth was delayed. And Scripture did not wish to say \"Shem, Japheth, and Ham,\" for then all of them would have been mentioned out of the order of their generations, and Japheth has no distinction that would overturn the order on his account. Rather, Shem was placed first on account of his distinction even though he is later in the account of the generations (Genesis 10:21). And similarly, \"the sons of Abraham: Isaac and Ishmael\" (I Chronicles 1:28), and similarly, \"and I gave to Isaac Jacob and Esau\" (Joshua 24:4)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:25:27.769026974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}